# Markdown rules

> Applies to: `**/*.md`, `**/*.mdx`, `docs/**`
> Toolchain version: CommonMark + GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM)  ·  Package manager: pnpm (Node 20)

## Commands (run from repo root)

| Purpose        | Command                                          |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| Install deps   | `pnpm install`                                   |
| Build          | N/A                                              |
| Run (dev)      | N/A                                              |
| Test (all)     | `pnpm exec markdownlint-cli2 "**/*.md"`          |
| Test (single)  | `pnpm exec markdownlint-cli2 path/to/file.md`    |
| Lint           | `pnpm exec markdownlint-cli2 "**/*.md"`          |
| Format         | `pnpm exec prettier --write "**/*.md"`           |
| Typecheck      | N/A                                              |

- `prettier` is **authoritative** for formatting — don't hand-format; run it.
- Before declaring done: run format and lint (see root DoD). Also verify links resolve.

## Style & structure

- Config lives in `.markdownlint.jsonc` and `.prettierrc` — don't override inline unless noted there.
- Naming: file names in `kebab-case.md`; one top-level `#` heading (H1) per document.
- Layout: headings increment by one level at a time (no skipping H2→H4); keep files focused and < 300 LOC per root rule — split long docs.
- Use ATX headings (`#`), fenced code blocks with a language tag, and reference-style links for repeated URLs.
- Wrap prose at a consistent width or leave one sentence per line — pick what the config enforces; don't mix.

## Errors & logging

- N/A for content. For code samples inside fenced blocks, show correct fail-fast idioms — no empty `catch`/silent fallbacks in examples (matches root rules).
- Never embed secrets, tokens, real credentials, or PII in examples; use obvious placeholders (`<YOUR_TOKEN>`).

## Testing

- Lint with `markdownlint-cli2`; every committed doc must pass with zero warnings.
- New/changed docs ship passing lint. Don't disable rules inline (`<!-- markdownlint-disable -->`) to make lint green unless justified in the PR.
- Verify all internal links and image paths resolve; check code fences specify a language.

## Dependencies

- Add tooling via `pnpm add -D <pkg>`; commit `pnpm-lock.yaml`.
- Pin versions via the lockfile; prefer maintained, permissively licensed tools.
- Qualify a new dependency with the user before adding it (root rule).
- Do not hand-edit generated files: `pnpm-lock.yaml`, any auto-generated tables of contents or API docs (regenerate instead).

## Language-specific gotchas

- Blank lines matter: fenced code blocks, lists, and headings need a surrounding blank line or they render wrong in GFM.
- Raw HTML is allowed in Markdown but sanitized by many renderers — prefer Markdown syntax; test rendering if HTML is required.
- Tables need a header row and `---` separator; misaligned pipes silently break the table.
- Trailing spaces for line breaks are error-prone — use explicit blank lines or `<br>` where a hard break is truly needed.
- MDX (`.mdx`) treats `{}` and `<Tag>` as JSX — escape literal braces/angle brackets or they'll fail to parse.
